Let \(C\subseteq\mathbb R^n\) be nonempty, closed, and convex and let \(T\) be compact. Suppose every \(f(\cdot,t)\) is convex and differentiable and that \(f\) and \(
abla_xf\) are continuous on \(C	imes T\). For \(\phi(x)=\max_{t\in T}f(x,t)\), \[\partial\phi(x)=\operatorname{conv}\{
abla_xf(x,t):t\in T(x)\}.\] Consequently, \(x^*\in C\) is globally optimal if and only if \[0\in\operatorname{conv}\{
abla_xf(x^*,t):t\in T(x^*)\}+N_C(x^*).\]
